# tally 2.2.1, E §11 REQ-CLOCK: "a cut an ask's literal states after `on` (`as known`, `with known`; a literal in `( )`
# too), in an ask load left standing" refuses the request, the run's one result, exit 1.
# 233.3: a member's ask c.qc, checked against its member's on (L §6.1, 228.Q10). tally 2.2 answered it RUN-DOMAIN,
# exit 0 (T's held fixes/member-clock).
=== options exit=1
=== c.tally
model cee
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "a card"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input pay: money PLN

input spare: num

def twice: money PLN = pay + pay at reader

ask q: twice law 2026-03-01





ask qw: twice with pay = 1 000.00 PLN law 2026-03-01

ask qk: twice law 2026-03-01 as known 2026-01-01

ask qc: twice law 2026-03-01 as known 2026-06-01

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pay = 4 000.00 PLN "the card"
=== jc.tally
model famc
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use c = "c.tally" sha256 "4e30fd4e96924dd31a5bc852efc3520aabe4df2976202d16323f154e3f9c0067"
